  "priorExpiration": "2020-03-31",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 2905.01 Application Process.\n\n(a) Applicants shall complete and submit “Law Enforcement Substance Abuse Reduction Initiative Application”, DSAD 67, (rev. 05/20), for consideration of a grant award.\n\n(b) DSAD 67, (rev. 05/20), may be downloaded from https://www.nh.gov/safety/divisions/homeland/index.html.\n\n(c) Applications shall only be submitted online to the email address provided in (d) below. Hard copies or facsimiles shall not be accepted.\n\n(d) Completed applications shall be submitted by emailing Homelandgrants@dos.nh.gov no later than 30 days after the announcement of the availability of grant funds made by the department of safety through a posting on the department’s website and electronic messaging to New Hampshire law enforcement agencies by the IAC. Applications received after the deadline shall be summarily rejected.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Saf-C 2900) #11150, EXEMPT, eff 8-5-16; ss by #12227, EXEMPT, eff 6-29-17; ss by #12527, eff 5-11-18; ss by #12894, EMERGENCY RULE, eff 10-3-19, EXPIRED: 3-31-20\n\nNew. #13230, eff 7-9-21",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c2900.html"
